A file named explicitly next to its directory is listed in the glob view even though the `.gitignore` ignores it. `input/.git/HEAD` makes `input` a git repository: outln applies `.gitignore` files only inside one.
== args
input/src
input/src/generated.md
== file input/.git/HEAD
ref: refs/heads/main
== file input/.gitignore
generated.md
== file input/src/a.md
---
description: A summary.
---
# a
== file input/src/generated.md
---
description: Explicitly named, so listed despite .gitignore.
---
# generated
== stdout
glob view: input/src input/src/generated.md
input/src/a.md (4 lines): description: "A summary."
input/src/generated.md (4 lines): description: "Explicitly named, so listed despite .gitignore."
